@page "/components/signature"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.Signature

<DocsHeader Title="Signature" Eyebrow="Capture">
    <Lead>A signature drawn with a finger, pen or mouse, or typed, for check-ins, deliveries and inspections.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<StilAlert Variant="StilVariant.Info" Appearance="StilAlertAppearance.Subtle">
    This is a picture of a signature to keep with a record. It is not a qualified electronic signature (such as one under
    the EU's eIDAS rules) and does not prove who signed. For agreements that need that, use an e-signing service.
</StilAlert>

<h2 id="form">In a form</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(SignedVisit)">
    <p>
        <code>StilSignaturePad</code> binds a <code>StilSignature</code> that is null until something is drawn or typed,
        so <code>[Required]</code> makes the signature required. Strokes are as wide as the pen presses. Undo removes the
        last stroke and Clear all of them. <strong>Type</strong> is the keyboard alternative: the signer types their name,
        shown in a handwriting font. The area is 10rem high; set <code>--stil-signature-height</code> to change it. Needs
        an interactive render mode.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="saving">Saving it</h2>
<p>
    A <code>StilSignature</code> has the <code>Strokes</code> (points with <code>X</code>, <code>Y</code> and
    <code>Pressure</code>), or the <code>TypedName</code>, and the <code>Width</code> and <code>Height</code> of the area.
    Store it as JSON, or as an image: <code>ToSvg(color)</code> in C# (also on the server), or
    <code>ToPngAsync(color)</code> on the pad, which draws it in the browser at twice its size. Both are dark ink on a
    transparent background unless you pass a color.
</p>

